    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d363">

                <pb facs="0371" n="359" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg359"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24591/38: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Ford</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-06T17:00:00+03:25">June 6, 1944—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 6—1:18 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>404. Department’s 315, May 20. Prime Minister<anchor n="24" xml:id="d363-f1"/>
                    states that suggestions regarding troop agreement which Shayesteh sent by mail
                    have never been received. Iranian Government still desires to conclude agreement
                    and has prepared new proposals to be carried to Washington by Ebtahaj<anchor
                        n="25" xml:id="d363-f2"/> this month for delivery to Shayestah.</p>
                <p>Prime Minister is unwilling to consider agreement on criminal jurisdiction over
                    troops until after conclusion of the general agreement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ford</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d363-f1" n="24" xml:id="d363-f1-content">
                <p>Mohammed Saed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d363-f2" n="25" xml:id="d363-f2-content">
                <p>Abol Hassan Ebtehaj, Director of the Central Bank (Banque Mellie) of Iran.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
